  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Transition to E-mobility in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the Government of Rwanda in its efforts to phase-out combustible engines and to facilitate a large-scale transition to e-mobility by building upon GGGI Rwanda&#x2019;s past work on green cities and EV charging infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transport has been identified as the main contributors to air pollution in Rwanda&#x2019;s fast-growing urban centers according to the Inventory of the Sources of Air Pollution in Rwanda. The project would have a significant impact on reducing air pollution, poverty reduction, inclusion, and the creation of green jobs.[1] The project aims to make several, targeted and measurable improvements to the enabling environment to foster the development the e-mobility sector including supplying the technical assistance required for the introduction of electric buses and required charging infrastructure within the City of Kigali with the opportunity to replicate pilot projects in the secondary cities.</narrative>
  </description>
